This is one of the most important requirements.

I want customer profiles and conversation history to be stored persistently in the project’s database, not only in the AI’s temporary context, browser memory, or current chat session.

The system must remember the information I provide about each customer and make it available in future sessions.

For every customer, maintain a structured profile containing the following fields when known:

IDENTITY

* Internal customer ID.
* Four-digit identifier.
* Customer name or assigned alias.
* Full name, if provided.
* Contact information, only when necessary and authorized.
* Date the profile was created.
* Last activity date.

RENTAL PREFERENCES

* Preferred city and area.
* Preferred neighborhoods or ZIP codes.
* Number of bedrooms.
* Number of bathrooms.
* Maximum monthly rent.
* Preferred property type: house, townhouse, apartment, condo, duplex, or other.
* Preferred move-in date or timeframe.
* Pet requirements.
* Garage, basement, fenced yard, laundry, accessibility, school district, or other requested features.
* Transportation or location restrictions.
* Other property-specific requirements.

APPLICATION AND RENTAL CONTEXT

* Properties the customer has expressed interest in.
* Property addresses and listing IDs, when available.
* Property links already sent.
* Whether a property is available, unavailable, or awaiting confirmation.
* Whether the customer has applied.
* Application status, if confirmed.
* Application fee status, if confirmed.
* Payment status, if confirmed.
* Application review status.
* Additional documents requested.
* Viewing or tour status.
* Holding or reservation status, when applicable.
* Outstanding questions or concerns.
* Next action required.

RENTAL HISTORY AND QUALIFICATION CONTEXT

* Credit concerns voluntarily disclosed by the customer.
* Previous evictions, if disclosed.
* Broken leases or rental balances, if disclosed.
* Rental history.
* Income or employment information, if disclosed and relevant.
* Other circumstances the customer wants us to consider.

Store sensitive information only when necessary for the rental workflow, with appropriate access controls. Do not store payment credentials, passwords, full bank details, or unnecessary sensitive documents in conversational memory.

CONVERSATION HISTORY

* Every customer message I enter.
* Every AI-generated response that I approve or send.
* Important decisions and corrections.
* Property recommendations sent.
* Customer feedback about recommendations.
* Questions already answered.
* Promises or follow-up dates.
* Unresolved concerns.
* The most recent state of the conversation.

The system must distinguish between information supplied by the customer, information supplied by me, and information inferred by the AI.

Do not treat assumptions as confirmed facts.

For example, if the customer says they applied but I have not confirmed the application status, record that the customer reported applying. Do not automatically mark the application as submitted in the actual application system.

