9. GUARANTORS, CO-SIGNERS, AND THIRD-PARTY APPLICATION SUPPORT

I want the system to support our legitimate application-assistance process, including situations in which a guarantor or co-signer may be appropriate.

However, do not invent a guarantor arrangement or automatically promise that we can attach another person’s credit or information to an application.

The AI must first determine what the company actually offers, what the property owner permits, and what the property’s application rules allow.

If Choice Properties has an approved guarantor or co-signer program, the knowledge base should document:

* Whether the program is available.
* Who qualifies to participate.
* Whether the guarantor or co-signer must submit a separate application.
* What consent and documentation are required.
* Whether the property owner accepts the arrangement.
* Whether any additional fee applies.
* Who is legally responsible for the lease.
* How the arrangement is disclosed to the property owner and screening provider.

A guarantor or co-signer must be a real, consenting person whose information is accurately represented.

Never instruct the AI to misrepresent an applicant, attach another person’s credit information without authorization, conceal who will occupy the property, or bypass screening requirements.

If the availability of a guarantor arrangement is not confirmed, the AI should explain that the application will be reviewed and that any permitted supporting options will be communicated during the process.

Do not state that a guarantor will be added automatically unless that is a verified, authorized business procedure.

